   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[{\"id\":\"T1110\",\"name\":\"Brute Force\",\"tactics\":[\"Credential Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert shows 5 failed login attempts against a single account, which is consistent with brute force attack patterns attempting to gain unauthorized access.\"},{\"id\":\"T1110.001\",\"name\":\"Password Guessing\",\"tactics\":[\"Credential Access\"],\"why_relevant\":\"Multiple failed LDAP authentication attempts indicate an adversary systematically guessing passwords to compromise the alopez account, a tactic explicitly mentioned in this technique.\"},{\"id\":\"T1078\",\"name\":\"Valid Accounts\",\"tactics\":[\"Initial Access\",\"Persistence\",\"Privilege Escalation\",\"Stealth\"],\"why_relevant\":\"The alert targets a valid domain account (alopez) that could be leveraged for initial access or privilege escalation if compromised through the failed login attempts.\"}],\"identity_signals\":{\"impossible_travel\":false,\"mfa_fatigue\":false,\"privilege_escalation\":false,\"dormant_account_reactivation\":false,\"notes\":\"Account alopez was locked after 5 failed LDAP authentication attempts from 172.16.0.88. No impossible travel, MFA fatigue, privilege escalation, or dormant account reactivation signals detected.\"},\"key_findings\":\"An external source (172.16.0.88) attempted a brute force attack against the valid domain account alopez with 5 failed LDAP login attempts, triggering account lockout. The attack was contained by the account lockout mechanism and no identity anomalies were detected. No evidence indicates the attacker gained internal access or account compromise.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"This is a blocked credential access attack from an external source (172.16.0.88). The account lockout control successfully prevented further unauthorized access attempts, and no internal compromise or identity anomalies were detected. While this represents a credible attack attempt, the defensive control functioned as intended and contained the threat at the perimeter.\",\"confidence\":0.85,\"recommended_response\":\"1) Verify the source IP 172.16.0.88 for malicious reputation and determine if it should be blocked at the perimeter. 2) Confirm the account lockout was triggered by this brute force attempt and not legitimate failed logins by alopez. 3) Contact user alopez to verify they did not attempt these logins and advise them to verify their last successful login time. 4) After verification, unlock the account and monitor for any additional suspicious login attempts. 5) Consider implementing rate limiting on LDAP authentication or enforcing account lockout policies if not already in place.\",\"rounds_used\":1}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
