     "text": "{\"related_campaigns\": [], \"kill_chain_stage\": \"credential access\", \"prior_alert_context\": \"This brute force event is typically an early-stage attack indicator. Expect to see subsequent alerts showing: (1) successful authentication if the attacker guesses correctly or uses credential spray tactics; (2) lateral movement attempts once valid credentials are obtained; (3) account enumeration or other post-compromise reconnaissance activities. The account lockout status suggests defensive mechanisms are functioning, but continued attempts against this or other accounts could indicate a larger credential access campaign. Monitor for similar failed login patterns against other high-value accounts (admin, service accounts) on the same system or domain within the next few hours.\", \"threat_severity_hint\": \"medium\"}",
