     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.75, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.8, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid triage with good foundational analysis. The investigator correctly identified the brute force attack, cited relevant ATT&CK techniques, and provided a defensible medium severity rating backed by the fact that the lockout control functioned as intended. The recommended actions are thorough and practical. Minor areas for improvement: (1) T1078 (Valid Accounts) citation could be strengthened by explicitly noting that the attacker targeted a confirmed valid account, making it relevant to the technique's use in post-compromise scenarios, though it's marginal here since there's no evidence of actual compromise; (2) the confidence score of 0.0 is jarring and unexplained\u2014clarify whether this refers to compromise confidence or attack confidence, as the narrative clearly shows high confidence in the brute force attack itself; (3) add one sentence confirming the source IP 172.16.0.88 is external/not a known internal subnet to fully justify the 'external source' assertion. Overall, this passes review and demonstrates competent threat analysis with appropriate containment assessment.\"}",
